   $q$What is the overall structure of this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Time order, telling the history of the town of Marlow year by year","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"Compare and contrast, showing how two rivers are alike and different","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"Problem and solution, telling how the town built a wall to stop floods","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Cause and effect, explaining why the river rises and what happens next","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Cause and effect, explaining why the river rises and what happens next$q$, $q$The passage asks "What causes this to happen?" and then explains causes (snow and rain) and effects (closed roads, rich soil). The town never builds a wall, so that choice is not supported.$q$, 'draft', '814bbb48-1c10-56de-9ddf-22ab2d6ce631')
