   $q$What is the theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Running fast is the best way to get a kite into the air.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-of-theme"},{"text":"Being patient and gentle can work better than forcing things.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Grandparents always know the answer to every problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Kites fly much better in summer than they do in spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Being patient and gentle can work better than forcing things.$q$, $q$Yanking the kite makes it fall, but waiting and letting out string makes it rise. Running fast is what failed in the first stanza, so that choice is the opposite of the lesson.$q$, 'draft', '60380577-c54a-532a-8e39-a499db1f8741')
