insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('512e5387-f430-5156-a9d8-0dc70dbb0ce5', 'rg4-theme-summary-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-theme-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Green Circle$q$, $q$Theo's grandfather, Pop Eli, had just gotten his first tablet. He wanted to video call Theo's cousin Zara, who lived far away. But every time he tried, he pressed the wrong button.

"This thing is impossible," Pop Eli grumbled.

Theo wanted to grab the tablet and do it himself. It would take him two seconds. Instead, he sat down beside his grandfather. "Let's go slow," he said. "First, find the green circle."

They practiced again and again. Pop Eli wrote each step on a card in big letters. On the fourth try, Zara's face popped onto the screen. "Pop Eli!" she cheered. Pop Eli laughed so hard his glasses slid down his nose.

After the call, Pop Eli pulled a wooden box from the closet. Inside was an old chess set with smooth, carved pieces. "Your turn to learn something," he said.

Theo had never played chess. The rules seemed confusing. The knight moved in a strange L shape, and he kept forgetting how. He felt his face get hot. He wanted to say the game was impossible.

Then he looked at the card on the table. GREEN CIRCLE, it said, in Pop Eli's big letters.

Theo took a breath. "Can we go slow?" he asked.

Pop Eli smiled. "That's the only way I know," he said.$q$, 'draft')
