   $q$The Greek root auto means "self," and graph means "write." What did Daniel hope to get when he wanted Ms. Farrow's "autograph"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A picture of her hometown to keep at home","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-with-photograph"},{"text":"A brand new copy of her newest story book","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Her name written by her own hand in his book","is_correct":true},{"text":"A short story she would write just for him","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her name written by her own hand in his book$q$, $q$An autograph is something a person writes themself, usually their own name, and Ms. Farrow signed her name in his book. The picture of her town was a photograph, not an autograph.$q$, 'draft', '8810dbb2-7977-552a-9fa2-57b075d92206')
