   $q$The suffix -less means "without." What are "flightless birds"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Birds that have no feathers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"Birds that fly very long ways","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Birds that swim in icy water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Birds that are not able to fly","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Birds that are not able to fly$q$, $q$Flightless means "without flight," and the next sentence says penguins cannot fly. Swimming is true of penguins, but it is not what the word flightless means.$q$, 'draft', 'b654ee9c-5516-5f64-accf-ac06a3ee8a71')
