-- Passage rg4-word-parts-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('144c885f-085e-5192-8306-379f7260aaab', 'rg4-word-parts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Machines That Help Themselves$q$, $q$Have you ever walked toward a store and watched the doors slide open by themselves? These are automatic doors. A small sensor above the door notices when someone comes near. Then a motor pulls the doors apart.

Many machines today work without a person controlling every step. Airplanes have an autopilot. It can keep the plane flying straight and steady while the pilots check their maps. Some ovens can preheat at a set time, so they are hot when the cook is ready.

Many of these machines run on batteries. A rechargeable battery can be filled with power over and over. This keeps old batteries out of the trash.

Still, machines are not perfect. A sensor can be fooled by dust or bright light. A door might stay shut, or an oven might get too hot. That is why engineers test their designs carefully. They look for any part that could misfire and fix it before the machine is sold.

Helpful machines save people time and energy. But people still need to check on them and keep them working safely.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
