   $q$What is the author's main point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Brookside should have students go to recess before they eat lunch.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ridgeview School has fewer lunchroom arguments than Brookside.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Brookside students should be allowed more time to play at recess.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Students at Brookside are too tired to eat after playing outside.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Brookside should have students go to recess before they eat lunch.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says "Recess should come before lunch," and the ending repeats that Brookside should try it. Being too tired to eat is what other people say, and the author answers it.$q$, 'draft', 'cc28ead5-37a5-5801-bf08-7a4658d089d5')
