insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('afec46de-636e-55b9-bd5f-cce2fa3a06ef', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$When the Canal Came to Millbrook$q$, $q$Account 1: Diary of Ezra Collins, Canal Boat Owner, 1838

May 3. The canal is finally open! This morning my boat carried forty barrels of flour toward the city. Two mules pulled us along the towpath at a steady walk. The trip will take three days, but a wagon takes a whole week. Millbrook is busier than I have ever seen it. A new inn is going up near the dock, and travelers fill the streets. I believe our little town will soon be a great one.

Account 2: Letter from Margarethe Vogel, Wagon Driver, 1838

Dear Sister,

These have been hard months for my family. Since the canal opened, the millers ship their flour by boat because it is faster and cheaper. I have had to sell two of my four wagons. Still, the canal cannot go everywhere. Farms far from the water still need my wagons to bring in seed and tools. Also, the canal freezes solid in winter. When the boats stop, the millers will come knocking at my door again. I will not give up yet.$q$, 'draft')
