-- Passage rg5-authors-purpose-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d2ec0f4e-9f70-5dd4-a10a-cc16fed43019', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Music in the Rain$q$, $q$Account 1: Journal of Yusuf Rahman, Age 12, Youth Orchestra Trumpet

Our summer concert in the park started under sunny skies. Then, in the middle of our second song, rain began to pour. My sheet music got soaked and the notes started to run. Our conductor waved us under the pavilion roof, and we kept going. We were squeezed so close that my elbow bumped the flute player. I have never felt so proud to finish a concert.

Account 2: Letter from Grace Whitfield, Audience Member

I sat on a blanket with my umbrella while the young musicians crowded under the pavilion roof. The rain drummed so loudly on my umbrella that I missed some of the quiet parts. Still, I loved watching those children keep playing. A few little ones in the crowd even danced in the puddles. It was the happiest wet evening I can remember.

Account 3: Report by Lucia Fernandez, Stage Manager

The forecast showed only a small chance of rain, so we set up on the open lawn. When the storm arrived, we moved the musicians under the pavilion. It fits only 40 of our 60 players, so the harp and piano stayed covered on the lawn. Without them, we had to cut two pieces from the program. Next year, I recommend renting a large tent as a backup.$q$, 'draft')
