-- Passage rg5-character-setting-plot-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('13d9af05-2d0d-5573-905c-f78a0b7a7f3a', 'rg5-character-setting-plot-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Fossil Dig$q$, $q$Nadia Haddad and her younger brother Omar spent a hot July week at a fossil dig in the desert. A scientist named Dr. Lindqvist showed them how to brush away dirt one thin layer at a time.

Nadia wanted to find a dinosaur. She chose a spot near a big rock and dug as deep as she could. Every few minutes she stopped to wipe her face and ask, "Is this a bone?" Each time, Dr. Lindqvist shook her head. It was only stone.

Omar picked a flat patch of ground and worked slowly. He liked the soft scratch of the brush. He found tiny gray shapes no bigger than his fingernail and set each one in a tray. Most were bits of shell.

On the fourth day, Nadia threw down her brush. "There's nothing here," she grumbled.

Dr. Lindqvist knelt beside Omar's tray. She held up a small curved shape under a magnifying glass. "This is a fish tooth," she said. "It means this desert was once the bottom of a lake."

Nadia leaned in to look. A lake, right where she was standing! The dry sand around her suddenly seemed full of secrets.

For the rest of the week, Nadia dug next to Omar. She did not find a dinosaur. But she found three fish teeth and a snail shell, and she labeled every one.$q$, 'draft')
