   $q$How does Luis's attitude toward Hana's ideas change from the beginning to the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He ignores her the whole time and takes credit for the triangles.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He likes her sketch at first, but later he decides paint matters more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-change"},{"text":"He calls her triangles messy at first, but later he wants to start with her sketch.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He agrees with her at first, but he stops listening after the bridge breaks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-change"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He calls her triangles messy at first, but later he wants to start with her sketch.$q$, $q$At first Luis "said they would look messy," but at the end he points at the triangles and says, "we start with your sketch." He gives Hana credit, so he does not ignore her.$q$, 'draft', '990273d6-2c1e-54fc-a5d9-07364f7585d2')
