        '3-5', $q$Two Small Mysteries$q$, $q$Text 1: The Paint Mystery (a mystery story)

On Monday morning, the art room was a mess. Three jars of blue paint lay tipped over on the floor. "Leo was the last one here on Friday," said Brenna. "He must have done it."

Leo's face turned red. "I closed every jar," he said quietly.

Ana did not say anything yet. She knelt by the puddles of paint. Small blue paw prints led across the floor to the window, which was open a crack. On the sill sat a few gray hairs.

"A cat got in over the weekend," Ana said, pointing to the prints. Brenna looked, then turned to Leo. "I'm sorry I blamed you," she said.

Text 2: The Case of the Missing Glasses (a mystery story)

Grandma Setsuko could not find her reading glasses anywhere. "Kenji was playing pirates with them yesterday," said his big sister, Yumi. "He probably hid them." Kenji, who was six, began to cry.

Their cousin Hana held up her hand. "Let's not guess. Grandma, what did you do after lunch?"

Grandma thought. "I read the newspaper. Then I put away the groceries."

Hana walked to the kitchen and opened the freezer. There, next to a carton of mango ice cream, were the glasses. Grandma laughed so hard she had to sit down. "The thief was me!" she said. Yumi gave Kenji a hug.$q$, 'draft')
